Is that an error message, or a warning?

If a correlation (or covariance) matrix can be created from real data (where one more variable(s) is not a linear sum of others), then it has eigenvalues that are all above zero. 1e-05 is so close to zero that it is essentially zero.

Are the variables b, c, d, f, h, i, k, l used in the model?

The program is telling you that it found a solution, but the solution found a covariance matrix that shoudn't be able to exist. That means that the model is probably wrong.

Jeremy

