Hi lavaan users,

```

I also noticed that your using ordered variables; therefore, you do not
need to specify the intercepts (this may very well be the reason why you
 get the error using older versions of lavaan); remove them from the
model;

```
I specified a first-stage moderated mediation model following the example given here: https://psu-psychology.github.io/psy-597-SEM/11_mediation_moderation/mediation_moderation_demo.html#first-stage-moderated-mediation

However, one of my endogeneous variables is binary and therefore I declared it as 'ordered'. To estimate the indirect effects conditional on the moderator, I need to specify the intercept, which results in the error message discussed here. Is there another way to specify the indirect effects conditional on the moderator than suggested in Hallquist's code (e.g., that cirumvents specifying the intercept)?

Thanks,
Melanie

